      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a largely structural change to SkAAClip that I wanted to land before I update it to use SkClipOp instead of SkRegion::Op. SkAAClip\u0027s public header leaked a lot of functionality so this reorganizes the functions and declarations to hide more of it in the cpp file. \n\nAdditionally, within the CPP file, static helper functions were migrated to be local inlinable lambdas when possible or moved into the anonymous namespace at the top of the file. Most definitions for SkAAClip were re-arranged w/o major changes to better match the declaration order and grouping in the header, along with moving the internal classes like Builder, Iter, etc. to be before any SkAAClip definitions.\n\nSince many of these functions and internal types are large blocks of code, the gerrit differ isn\u0027t the most helpful, so I tried making notes of what things were simply moved and calling out slightly more substantive tweaks. That being said, this shouldn\u0027t have any behavioral changes in it, it\u0027s all reorg work.",
      "revId": "dfbfa329dcfaa6dcb2c82b582c2040424c536497",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
