      "writtenOn": "2021-09-03T18:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are simple abstractions over the previous way that Builder was used. A Builder would be created, then operated on, and then \"finished\" into a target SkAAClip. For the setPath case, it would also have to create a Blitter that had to be finished before the Builder. Now Builder can handle all of that logic within these functions and make most of its API private.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 308,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "dfbfa329dcfaa6dcb2c82b582c2040424c536497",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
